{"id": "853a22c2-8886-4941-9890-608859b54994", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T20:11:35.128394", "source": "agent", "parent_id": null, "system_prompt": {"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "Collaborate with the researcher to develop an experiment design for the original task. First inspect the masked repository and supplied inputs, then use end_researcher_turn with stage=plan to propose an approach, consequential choices and uncertainties. Wait for explicit researcher approval before developing the full design. After approval, hand off stage=result with the complete design in answer, supported by rationale, controls, feasible checks and repository observations in evidence. State assumptions separately from fixed task requirements. No executed experiment or invented outcome is required for this design-only task. Use inspect_repository and execute_check for exploration. Share concrete findings: private tool output is not automatically sent to the researcher. Revise when needed; do not invent objections or ambiguities to extend the conversation. The researcher decides when to stop."}, "tools": [{"description": "List a repository directory or read a text file. Paths are relative to the task workspace.", "action_type": "InspectRepositoryAction", "observation_type": "BenchmarkObservation", "annotations": null, "meta": null, "kind": "InspectRepositoryTool", "title": "inspect_repository"}, {"description": "Run a shell command in the isolated task workspace. Use small exploratory checks before submitting your plan.", "action_type": "ExecuteCheckAction", "observation_type": "BenchmarkObservation", "annotations": null, "meta": null, "kind": "ExecuteCheckTool", "title": "execute_check"}, {"description": "Yield a proposed approach (stage=plan) or completed experiment design (stage=result), with evidence, assumptions and uncertainties. The researcher decides when to finish.", "action_type": "ReviewHandoffAction", "observation_type": "BenchmarkObservation", "annotations": null, "meta": null, "kind": "ReviewHandoffTool", "title": "end_researcher_turn"}], "dynamic_context": {"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "<CURRENT_DATETIME>\nThe current date and time is: 2026-10-22T20:11\n</CURRENT_DATETIME>"}, "kind": "SystemPromptEvent"}
{"id": "8f1f8d02-75bd-46fd-9428-2e98884f56ef", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T20:11:35.131019", "source": "user", "parent_id": "853a22c2-8886-4941-9890-608859b54994", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"नमस्ते। इस turn पर सिर्फ़ inspection और proposed approach चाहिए — पूरा design अभी मत दीजिए।\\n\\nकृपया ये करें:\\n1. Repository (या उपलब्ध InfLLM स्रोत सामग्री) का सिर्फ़ structured inspection: InfLLM का retrieved-memory pipeline कहाँ है — (a) context memory बनाने/writing का code, (b) memory lookup या retrieval का step (block selection, similarity scoring, top-k retrieval), (c) unit representation चुनने की जगह (block summary / memory unit के रूप में raw tokens बनाम pooled/clustered/learned representations), और (d) configuration knobs जो ये दोनों चीज़ें control करते हैं (block size, retrieval budget, number of retrieved units, representation type)।\\n2. उसी आधार पर एक संक्षिप्त proposed experimental approach: dynamic context memory lookup और unit representation के effect को अलग-अलग (factorially) कैसे isolate करेंगे, कौन-से long-context task families पर, कौन-से controls/baselines से (जैसे full attention upper bound, no-retrieval/local-window lower bound, fixed/static retrieval vs dynamic), और कौन-से metrics से — सिर्फ़ bullet-level rationale, विस्तृत protocol नहीं।\\n3. Explicit assumptions और uncertainties की सूची: कौन-सा setup detail source में स्पष्ट नहीं है (उदा. InfLLM का कौन-सा version/base model, कौन-से benchmarks, retrieval mechanism का exact form, k/budget values, compute budget) — इन्हें assumption के तौर पर label कीजिए, confirmed fact मत बताइए।\\n\\nअगर कोई file/module source में मौजूद नहीं है तो सीधे \\\"not present\\\" कहिए; अनुमान से code structure मत गढ़िए। Execution इस task में required नहीं है — deliverable design + rationale + controls + analysis plan + feasibility है, इसलिए कृपया inspect-only और approach proposal पर ही रुकिए।\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"How critical are dynamic context memory lookup and the choice of unit representations to InfLLM’s performance across long-context tasks?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 224, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null, "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "critic_result": null, "kind": "MessageEvent"}
